Z||000001||HYPTNOTiSE||05-31-2000||07:49 AM||||shane make sure you at least order polyurethane cradle bushings.  If i were you'd i'd get aluminum, any cradle movement is too much. Contact Morse86@aol.com for aluminum bushings,i believe they're 150-200 dollars||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||05-31-2000||10:51 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.suspension.com" TARGET=_blank>www.suspension.com</A>  Good price, good service, pay only actual shipping cost of parts.<P>the rears are easy as long as the captive nuts haven't been wrecked. the fronts need to be cut/burned out of the outer sleeve.||||reg||1
